    "name": "Bi-Color Corn",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Bi-color corn is a sweet corn variety featuring a mix of both yellow and white kernels on the same cob.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Taste Profile:</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\"> It is known for a sweet, rich flavor that combines the sugary taste of white corn with the traditional flavor of yellow corn. According to community consensus on </span><a href=\"https://www.quora.com/Is-bi-color-corn-on-the-cob-tastier-than-white-corn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"lexical-text-editor--link\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Quora</span></a><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">, users agree that overall flavor depends more on freshness, specific variety, and cooking method than just the color alone.</span></p>",
